  "description": "A database gateway that lets existing applications reach SQL Server and Azure SQL through an identity you control, and records everything they do - without changing the application or the database. Clients connect to DaffyTee as if it were SQL Server; it authenticates them with its own logins, logs in to the target as the identity mapped to each (a SQL login, or an Entra ID application for Azure SQL), follows Azure SQL redirects, and every request (SQL, parameters, user, timing, rows, errors) is streamed asynchronously to RabbitMQ or a file - for troubleshooting, performance analysis, security investigations, compliance and migration planning - without slowing the database path. Administered at its own prompt, or in T-SQL from SSMS (EXEC daffytee.help). Passwords are never logged. Early release.",
